PicoGKRuntime 26.2 (0f26321c) — opt-in adaptive meshing through a new export,
Mesh_hCreateFromVoxelsAdaptive. Spike S1 (branch spike/openvdb-adaptivity):
measured against the SG1 gate, not yet offered upstream.

Applied to vendor/PicoGKRuntime by scripts/fetch-deps.sh after 0001-0005.
Kept as a patch because it modifies dependency source; no flag-level override
exists.

1. Source/PicoGKVdbVoxels.h — roAsMesh() gains fAdaptivity (default 0). At 0
   the call is the one 0001 makes, VolumeToMesh(0, 0, false) with
   enableFlatQuadOutput(), so Mesh_hCreateFromVoxels keeps its bytes. Above 0
   it runs VolumeToMesh(0, fAdaptivity, true): OpenVDB's adaptive mesher merges
   near-coplanar cells and relaxes disoriented triangles (its default for
   adaptive meshing). The adaptive branch never takes the flat-quad path
   (VolumeToMesh selects it only for uniform, non-reference meshing), so the
   result is read through 0001's per-leaf pool path, triangles and quads.
2. API/PicoGK.h, Source/PicoGKLibrary.cpp — Mesh_hCreateFromVoxelsAdaptive
   (hInstance, hVoxels, fAdaptivity): NaN and values at or below 0 select the
   uniform mesher, values above 1 clamp to 1.

Evidence: Tau Brain run 2026-10-16-adaptivity-spike (lane adaptivity).
